      {
        "id": 44502,
        "name": "EvanDan55",
        "username": "EvanDan55",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/{size}/2374_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-19T20:33:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Actually, I took a look at La Capitan's nemesis icon again because I couldn't make it out before, and now, it gives me a little trouble. The icon is rather cluttered, having four distinct things on it, each rather different. There's a chain, an explosion of light, green circles, and what looks like the end of a black tornado. Can her nemesis not decide on a theme? What could this represent?</p><p>Perhaps there's a hero character card that features four distinct characters, who are played like a normal deck, but still represent four entities fighting at once? Of course, there'd still be one base power and one total HP, but four characters in that one deck.</p><p>But I think I'm looking too far into that. Maybe the symbol is just for a hero who is really indecisive.</p>",
        "post_number": 31,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:18:04.292Z",
