        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/c57346/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-19T20:43:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"evandan55\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/48/2374_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> evandan55:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Actually, I took a look at La Capitan's nemesis icon again because I couldn't make it out before, and now, it gives me a little trouble. The icon is rather cluttered, having four distinct things on it, each rather different. There's a chain, an explosion of light, green circles, and what looks like the end of a black tornado. Can her nemesis not decide on a theme? What could this represent?Perhaps there's a hero character card that features four distinct characters, who are played like a normal deck, but still represent four entities fighting at once? Of course, there'd still be one base power and one total HP, but four characters in that one deck.But I think I'm looking too far into that. Maybe the symbol is just for a hero who is really indecisive.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Based on the conjecture from another thread and your analysis of La Capitan's nemesis icon, I'm becoming more and more convinced that the hero is going to be some sort of shapeshifter.</p>",
